{"data": [{"author_id": "18596919", "created_at": "2026-10-25T22:01:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114477471085064519"], "id": "2114477471085064519", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 98, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "In 2001, about 72% of the world’s central bank reserves were held in dollars. Today it’s under 57%. The president and the vice president disagree on whether that’s a problem, and the answer turns on a question almost nobody in Washington is asking. 🧵", "url": "https://x.com/JonathanDever/status/2114477471085064519"}, {"author_id": "140446839", "created_at": "2026-10-25T22:53:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114490462035960263"], "id": "2114490462035960263", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "THE LIQUIDITY WARNING IS REAL.\n\nFed data: US bank reserves fell $59.5B in one week, while Treasury cash rose $68.6B.\n\nTighter liquidity could pressure both tech stocks and gold.\n\nA rebound doesn't erase the underlying risks.\n\n$NDX $XAUUSD #Nasdaq100", "url": "https://x.com/bobbytowira/status/2114490462035960263"}, {"author_id": "2070031994831196160", "created_at": "2026-10-26T05:00:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114582927522566172"], "id": "2114582927522566172", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 29, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Gold Is 24% of Central Bank Reserves, While Actual Buying Fell a Fifth\n\nExcluding the United States, gold's share of global central bank reserves has climbed back to about 24%, the highest since 2000. Around 2015 the same figure was close to 10%.\n\nThis is a share measured at https://t.co/4CgHki5Pe1", "url": "https://x.com/LearnInvest2026/status/2114582927522566172"}, {"author_id": "2030927462981607424", "created_at": "2026-10-26T02:35:25.000Z"